{%- comment -%}
  The loading state, shared by anything that has to wait: the quick view while
  the piece is fetched, the search overlay while a query is in flight, and
  whatever comes next. One mark, so a wait always looks the same.

  The mark is **the design's own diamond** — the brilliant cut it draws in its
  image placeholders (`Glorious All Products.dc.html`), path for path: the kite
  outline, the girdle rule across it, and the two crown facets. The design has
  no loading state of its own anywhere in its 24 pages, so the animation is
  ours; the shape is not, and should not be redrawn.

  What it does is draw itself: the outline is struck in one stroke, the facets
  catch the light once it closes, and the whole mark fades so it can be struck
  again. `pathLength="100"` is what makes that possible without measuring
  anything in JavaScript — it normalises every path to 100 units, so one
  `stroke-dasharray` in the stylesheet serves all three.

  Takes:
    label  what a screen reader announces. Defaults to `general.loading`.
    size   `sm`, `md` (default) or `lg`.

  It carries `role="status"`, so the label is announced when it appears — and
  it must therefore be *rendered into* the page at the moment of waiting rather
  than sitting there hidden, or nothing is announced at all.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign loader_label = label
  if loader_label == blank
    assign loader_label = 'general.loading' | t
  endif

  assign loader_size = size | default: 'md'
-%}

<span class="loader loader--{{ loader_size }}" role="status">
  <svg class="loader__mark" viewBox="32 30 36 41" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <path class="loader__cut" pathLength="100" d="M50 32l16 13-16 24-16-24z"></path>
    <path class="loader__facet" pathLength="100" d="M34 45h32"></path>
    <path class="loader__facet" pathLength="100" d="M50 32l-7 13 7 24 7-24z"></path>
  </svg>
  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ loader_label }}</span>
</span>
